@document
  title: All Features Demo
  author: Gemini

@meta
  user:
    name: Alice
    role: admin
    balance: 250.50
  items: [{"name": "Laptop", "price": 1200}, {"name": "Mouse", "price": 25}, {"name": "Monitor", "price": 300}]

@define Card(title="Info", footer="End of card")
  @box
    # {{title}}
    @slot
    
    *{{footer}}*

# All Features Demo

## 1. Rich Expressions
User: {{user.name}} ({{user.role}})  
Balance: ${{user.balance}}  
Bonus: ${{user.balance * 0.10}} (10%)  
Can Afford Laptop? {{user.balance >= 1200}}  

Math with spacing: 5 * 10 + 2 = {{5 * 10 + 2}}  

## 2. Advanced Control Flow
@if user.balance > 1000
  Status: Platinum
@elseif user.balance > 100
  Status: Gold
@else
  Status: Silver
@end

### Inventory
@foreach item in items
  {{loop.count}}. **{{item.name}}**: ${{item.price}}
  @if loop.first
    (Best Seller!)
  @elseif loop.last
    (Clearance!)
  @end
@end

Total Items: {{items.length}}  

## 3. Enhanced Macros
@use Card(title="User Profile")
  Name: {{user.name}}  
  Role: {{user.role}}
@end

@use Card()
  This card uses the default title.  
  It also has a default footer.
@end

@use Card(title="Custom Footer", footer="Copyright 2026")
  This card has a custom footer.
@end

## 4. New Markdown Features

### Blockquotes
> This is a blockquote.
> It is indented and has a border.

### Horizontal Rules
---

### Links
Visit [Google](https://google.com) or [OpenAI](https://openai.com).

### Inline Formatting
This is ~~deleted text~~ and this is `inline code`.

### Footnotes
Here is a footnote reference[^1].
And another one[^note].

[^1]: This is the first footnote definition.
[^note]: This is a named footnote definition.

